{"title":"Career Roadmap · IP Associate","role":"IP Associate","summary":"An IP Associate is a legal professional who works on intellectual property matters, including patents, trademarks, copyright, designs, trade secrets, licensing and technology-related transactions.","facts":{"Current degree":"Law – LLB / BA LLB / BBA LLB / B.Com LLB / B.Sc LLB (Integrated)","Course":"Science & Technology Law (B.Sc LLB)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An IP Associate is a legal professional who works on intellectual property matters, including patents, trademarks, copyright, designs, trade secrets, licensing and technology-related transactions."},{"type":"p","text":"For a student pursuing B.Sc LL.B. with a Science & Technology Law orientation, the combination of scientific understanding and legal training can be particularly useful in technology-heavy IP practices."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical work includes:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"IP legal research"},{"text":"Patent and trademark research"},{"text":"IP prosecution support"},{"text":"Patent specification review"},{"text":"Trademark applications"},{"text":"Copyright matters"},{"text":"IP licensing"},{"text":"Technology-transfer agreements"},{"text":"IP due diligence"},{"text":"IP portfolio management"},{"text":"Infringement analysis"},{"text":"IP litigation support"},{"text":"Technology contracts"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"An IP Associate is a broad professional role. Patent practice has additional statutory requirements in India. An LLB/B.Sc LL.B. graduate should not assume that the law degree alone qualifies them to act as a registered Patent Agent. Patent-agent practice requires satisfaction of the applicable technical/scientific eligibility and registration requirements."}]},{"heading":"Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Class 12","B.Sc LL.B. / Integrated Law Degree","Scie